  "summary": {
    "as": "Reported to House",
    "asOf": "2026-10-29",
    "date": "2026-11-12T20:17:59Z",
    "text": "Crossett Experimental Forest Act of 2026\n\nThis bill directs the Forest Service, upon the request of the State of Arkansas,\u00a0to convey the Crossett Experimental Forest, the R.R. Reynolds Research Natural Area, and associated facilities to the state.\u00a0\n\nUpon the conveyance, Arkansas must designate the land as the\u00a0Crossett Experimental State Forest. In order to retain the land, Arkansas must\n\nuse the land for forest research, education, and demonstration purposes in a manner consistent with the historic research mission of the forest; anduse the forest in coordination with the University of Arkansas at\u00a0Monticello and the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture, including by providing the universities with reasonable access to the forest for research and educational purposes.The bill outlines the terms and conditions of the conveyance, including requiring the conveyance to\u00a0be (1) subject to valid existing rights, (2) made without consideration (e.g., payment), and (3) made by\u00a0quitclaim deed.\n\nArkansas must pay the costs of the conveyance, including costs for surveys and other administrative costs."
  },
